  "chapter_name": "",
  "level": 1,
  "question": "Match the reactions in List-I with the features of their products in List-II and choose the correct option.\nList-I: (P) (–)-1-Bromo-2-ethylpentane (single enantiomer) $\\ce{->[aq. NaOH][S_N2 reaction]}$\n(Q) (–)-2-Bromopentane (single enantiomer) $\\ce{->[aq. NaOH][S_N2 reaction]}$\n(R) (–)-3-Bromo-3-methylhexane (single enantiomer) $\\ce{->[aq. NaOH][S_N1 reaction]}$\n(S) Compound shown in the figure (single enantiomer) $\\ce{->[aq. NaOH][S_N1 reaction]}$\nList-II: (1) Inversion of configuration (2) Retention of configuration (3) Mixture of enantiomers (4) Mixture of structural isomers (5) Mixture of diastereomers",
