  "chapter_name": "",
  "level": 1,
  "question": "$\\ce{C6H5-C(CH3)2-Br}$ in aqueous ethanol gives an acidic solution, whereas $p$-$\\ce{Br-C6H4-CH(CH3)2}$ in aqueous ethanol gives a neutral solution. The reason is",
  "option1": "both compounds hydrolyse, but HBr formed from the second one is neutralised by the ring",
  "option2": "$\\ce{C6H5C(CH3)2Br}$ ionises easily ($S_N1$, stable 3° benzylic carbocation) and releases HBr, whereas Br on the benzene ring is not replaced because the C–Br bond has partial double bond character",
  "option3": "$\\ce{C6H5C(CH3)2Br}$ is oxidised to benzoic acid, whereas the second compound is not oxidised",
