  "chapter_name": "",
  "level": 1,
  "question": "Cyclobutyl bromide on treatment with magnesium in dry ether forms an organometallic (A). The organometallic reacts with ethanal to give an alcohol (B) after mild acidification. Prolonged treatment of alcohol (B) with an equivalent amount of HBr gives 1-bromo-1-methylcyclopentane (C). Which of the following is correct?",
  "option1": "A = cyclobutyl bromide dimer; B = cyclobutanol; C forms by $S_N2$ substitution",
  "option2": "A = cyclobutylmagnesium bromide; B = 2-cyclobutylethanol; C forms by $S_N2$ substitution without rearrangement",
  "option3": "A = cyclobutylmagnesium bromide; B = cyclobutylmethanol; C forms by hydride shift",
  "option4": "A = cyclobutylmagnesium bromide; B = 1-cyclobutylethanol; C forms through ring expansion of the 1-cyclobutylethyl cation to the more stable 1-methylcyclopentyl cation",
  "correct_option": "A = cyclobutylmagnesium bromide; B = 1-cyclobutylethanol; C forms through ring expansion of the 1-cyclobutylethyl cation to the more stable 1-methylcyclopentyl cation",
